  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v3.2.0 stable - first SpawnDev.WebTorrent minor cut since 3.1.0. Bundles five additive features on top of 3.1.7's wire-level seeder correctness fix; zero behavior change for consumers who don't opt in to any of the new surfaces. (1) Inbound TCP listener wired as a first-class API: `WebTorrentClientOptions.TcpListenPort` (null/0/>0), `TcpListenAddress` (default `IPAddress.Any`), `WebTorrentClient.TcpListener` property + `EnsureTcpListenerAsync(port, address)` idempotent helper. Mainline clients (qBittorrent, libtorrent, Transmission, rqbit) can dial in by IP+port; listener peeks 68-byte BT handshake, routes by info_hash to the matching torrent. Full doc: `Docs/tcp-listener.md`. (2) Tracker advertising for the listener: opt-in `WebTorrentClientOptions.AdvertiseTcpListenerToTrackers` flag. When enabled, every HTTP / UDP tracker announce includes the listener's actual port in BEP 3 `port=` field so trackers put us in their compact peer list and mainline peers find us automatically (no manual `addPeers`). WebSocket tracker signaling is unaffected (WebRTC-only). (3) Pluggable piece-hash engine: new `IPieceHashEngine` interface + `SystemCryptoPieceHashEngine` default (System.Security.Cryptography). `WebTorrentClient.PieceHashEngine` property + `WebTorrentClientOptions.PieceHashEngine` slot-in let recheck-heavy workloads route through GPU / batched implementations without changing call sites. Default behavior (System.Security.Cryptography) is byte-identical to 3.1.x. (4) Bandwidth policy: new `BandwidthPolicy` enum (`Unlimited` / `Conservative` / `Metered` / `SeedingDisabled` / `Custom`) with translation through `WebTorrentClientOptions.BandwidthPolicy`. Conservative = 256 KiB/s upload ceiling, Metered = 64 KiB/s, SeedingDisabled = 0 (paused). Explicit `UploadLimit` always wins over the policy. Runtime knob: `WebTorrentClient.ApplyBandwidthPolicy(policy)`. (5) SipSorcery fork: `MediaStreamTrack.StreamStatus` setter widened from `internal` to `public` so consumers can flip direction post-construction without reflection or track recreation. Strict superset of upstream surface. New PlaywrightMultiTest coverage: 8 desktop tests across the five new surfaces. All shipped tests + interop matrix (qBittorrent live-swarm both directions, JS WebTorrent live-swarm via local SpawnDev.RTC tracker) green.",
